{"availability":"available","full":"Ramiriz-Leal/queue-agent-demo","name":"queue-agent-demo","description":"Desktop automation agent demo built with Tauri and React: lives in the system tray, polls a mocked job queue, processes one job at a time with a live log, and persists settings to a real config file. No backend and no network calls.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-09T12:08:32Z","updated":"2026-09-09T16:21:18Z","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["automation","desktop-app","react","rust","system-tray","tauri","typescript"],"demo":"https://tauri.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T22:40:00.156Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T22:40:00.156Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T22:40:00.156Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T22:40:00.156Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React","Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A fully working desktop application (Tauri + React) that demonstrates the shape of a background automation agent: it lives in the system tray, polls a mocked job queue on an interval, processes jobs one at a time with a live log, and exposes a Settings screen to control the AI model, effort level, working directory and polling behavior. Everything (the queue, the jobs, the settings) is simulated in memory and in a local config file. There is no external backend, no real queue, no real AI provider, and no network calls of any kind.","This project is a portfolio piece: it is not connected to, and does not depend on, any production system."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Ramiriz-Leal/queue-agent-demo/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"49f2ef8e9042bb564781a9e6732e8e734f0a0e7e808088878165ce8817faa9e8","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T22:40:00.308Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T22:40:00.308Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A fully working desktop application (Tauri + React) that demonstrates the shape of a bac